// Self-centered burst -- CharacterAbility::Explosion always detonates at
// the caster's own position (common/src/states/explosion.rs has no
// target-point field), which matches this spell's own "Self" range exactly
// (contrast acid_splash.ron, whose 18 m range forced a deviation to
// GroundAoe instead). Explosion also hardcodes DamageKind::Crushing in
// common/src/explosion.rs -- no RON-configurable damage_kind field exists
// on this variant -- so despite the Thunder flavor text this deals generic
// Crushing damage under the hood; the small Away knockback below still
// fits "concussive crack of sound" reasonably well as compensation.
//
// Damage is set below the batch's single-target cantrip baseline (14) since
// this can hit every creature in the radius at once, not just one -- the
// same AoE-cantrip discount real D&D itself applies (Thunderclap's actual
// die is 1d6, notably below a single-target cantrip's 1d10).
Explosion(
    energy_cost: 0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    action_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    damage: 10,
    poise: 8,
    knockback: (direction: Away, strength: 4.0),
    radius: 3.0,
    min_falloff: 0.3,
    dodgeable: Roll,
    destroy_terrain: None,
    eye_height: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
